      "message": "If req_immediate_exit is true, then we will make KVM_REQ_EVENT request to vcpu and request an immediate exit. In this case, this if condition will also be true, then we jump to handle_events to handle KVM_REQ_EVENT again. And if there is vcpu-\u003earch.nmi_pending and exception is already injected, then we will set req_immediate_exit to true, which seems like will fall into this loop again?\n\nAs if we have set req_immediate_exit, the host vm will exit immediately after injecting the pending event, probably we don\u0027t need to check the pending request if req_immediate_exit is true. Maybe we can do it in this way:\n\n```\nhandle_events:\n          handle_pending_events(vcpu, \u0026req_immediate_exit);\n          \n          set_vcpu_mode(vcpu, IN_GUEST_MODE);\n\n          if (req_immediate_exit) {\n                  kvm_make_request(KVM_REQ_EVENT, vcpu);\n                  request_host_immediate_exit(vmx);\n          } else if (vcpu-\u003emode \u003d\u003d EXITING_GUEST_MODE || kvm_request_pending(vcpu)) {\n                  goto handle_events;\n          }\n```\nHow do you think?",
